:question/worked-solution "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, and the two $\\sqrt{y}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt[3]{y}-4\\sqrt{y}-7\\sqrt[3]{y}+2\\sqrt{y} & = \\\\ (-4+2)\\sqrt{y}+(3-7)\\sqrt[3]{y} & = \\\\ -2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35580c97-b64e-55a3-b71e-9190dbcac10b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Sums of Radicals Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d7d654-83a6-5095-8350-0c24ed3b09f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563002} {:answer/id #uuid "3f460124-51cf-5f31-ae09-245b7c4d361f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563088} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0c664c-f8c9-5f53-b9f0-e91c57fa6455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563151} {:answer/id #uuid "8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563263} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fc2ea4-ed54-5789-9c1b-da6da0a36fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}-x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563263} :answer-field/id #uuid "2edd54bc-8785-50e5-9005-f3528fdfbcbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aceecb75-92cf-58b4-997d-d31ecad9d81f" :question/math-academy-id "q-29322" :question/problem "Simplify $2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9\\cdot 6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\cdot 3\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ (6x-5x)\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35580c97-b64e-55a3-b71e-9190dbcac10b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Sums of Radicals Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563245} {:answer/id #uuid "9026f5ff-791a-5770-911f-0b0b83b85fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-3x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563268} {:answer/id #uuid "9c93eb0d-6ded-596d-b4ab-b36cd01140e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563296} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5245bd-caba-5f74-b81d-55f9a9e8ac2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-x\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563336} {:answer/id #uuid "ebcfccec-dd55-5089-ac9a-b0ae93280f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}-{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563245} :answer-field/id #uuid "c61d8497-db30-5312-b6cc-cc9f8eeed283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a056777d-2d90-5391-b8e4-3c8ae89bd6c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-4064" :question/problem "$3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{27}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{27}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{5}} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{4}\\cdot x} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{4}}\\cdot \\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}-3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}-3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ (3-3)\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 0\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
